{title: A Witness on Their Lips}
{subtitle: Deuteronomy 31:14–21}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The day of your death is near
Summon Joshua, stand together
Present yourselves at the tent
Where I will commission him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I appeared in a pillar of cloud
Standing over the entrance
You lie down with your fathers soon
But the people will rise up
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Write down [F#]this song for your[C#]selves
Teach it to the [G#]Israe[F#]lites
[D#m]Put it in their [F#]mouths deep
[C#]So it stands [G#]as my [F#]witness
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They prostitute themselves to foreign gods
Forsaking me and my covenant
My anger will burn against them
I will hide my face away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Write down this [F#]song for your[C#]selves
Teach it to the [G#]Israe[F#]lites
[D#m]Put it in their [F#]mouths deep
[C#]So it stands [G#]as my wit[F#]ness
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
They eat their fill and grow fat
Then they despise my holy name
When disasters come upon them
They will say I am gone
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
This song will [F#]testify against [C#][G#][F#]them [D#m][F#][C#][G#][F#]
[D#m]It will not [F#]be lost from their [C#]lips
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [C#] [G#] [F#] | [D#m] [F#] | [C#] [G#] [F#] |
| [D#m] | ×13
